 ## Subtopics
+
+### [Multi-Frame Rate Volume Rendering](11326-multi-frame-rate-volume-rendering.md)
+Multi-frame rate volume rendering is an asynchronous parallel rendering technique that distributes workload across multiple GPUs to balance high frame rates with high visual quality. A fast display GPU handles user input and low-latency feedback, while one or more backend GPUs asynchronously compute high-quality views. It distinguishes itself from earlier multi-frame rate systems by using layered image warping to preserve motion parallax and enable view-dependent lighting for transparent volumetric structures, rather than reconstructing the scene as a single surface.
 
